WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.225
This is the heart of the proposal, and
it's the programmatic data knowledge.

2
00:00:04.225 --> 00:00:08.762
OPM already defines the personnel
data every agency records.

3
00:00:08.762 --> 00:00:12.912
Agency and subelement give the
legal employer and component.

4
00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:15.462
Duty station is the location of record.

5
00:00:15.462 --> 00:00:20.700
Series, pay plan and grade give a
position category for role-based access.

6
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:24.287
Supervisory status tells us
who can approve and review.

7
00:00:24.287 --> 00:00:27.451
Tenure and appointment type
drive the worker type.

8
00:00:27.451 --> 00:00:30.721
And the nature-of-action
code, with its effective date,

9
00:00:30.721 --> 00:00:33.100
tells us what just happened — next slide.

10
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:37.125
Why build on OPM's standard rather
than on Oracle's field names?

11
00:00:37.125 --> 00:00:40.983
Because OPM standards provide
a common federal vocabulary

12
00:00:40.983 --> 00:00:44.300
that agencies can map into
a shared canonical model.

13
00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:49.083
We map them to Entra ID and AD once,
for every employee population —

14
00:00:49.083 --> 00:00:53.325
and if the HR vendor ever
changes, the mapping still holds.

15
00:00:53.325 --> 00:00:57.650
One honest limit: HRIT covers
federal employees only.

16
00:00:57.650 --> 00:00:59.502
In the processes I have observed,

17
00:00:59.502 --> 00:01:02.863
contractors and vendors are
tracked in COR spreadsheets.

18
00:01:02.863 --> 00:01:05.752
A contractor authority
decision is required,

19
00:01:05.752 --> 00:01:08.946
and I propose evaluating
three candidate sources:

20
00:01:08.946 --> 00:01:12.064
Core HCM's Contingent Worker
type — a person record,

21
00:01:12.064 --> 00:01:15.410
an assignment and a lifecycle
much like an employee's,

22
00:01:15.410 --> 00:01:18.984
though with no vendor-management
layer; PIV sponsorship;

23
00:01:18.984 --> 00:01:21.494
and a contractor suitability register,

24
00:01:21.494 --> 00:01:26.437
which ties each contractor to an agency
contract with a suitability decision.

25
00:01:26.437 --> 00:01:29.550
That's a decision to put in
front of the program early.
